{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99ecce3eb56f1b57","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9012\n3\ttitle: Bundle an S3-compatible object store for disconnected installs\n4\tstatus: Refinement Done\n5\tpriority: Major\n6\tlabels:\n7\t- refined\n8\t- disconnected\n9\tlinks: []\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## Problem Statement\n13\t\n14\tPipelines and model serving both require S3-compatible object storage, but\n15\tdisconnected customers frequently have none. Field teams work around this by\n16\tinstalling upstream MinIO ad hoc — unsupported, unpatched, and invisible to the\n17\tplatform. We want a supported, bundled S3-compatible store that administrators\n18\tcan enable for disconnected and PoC clusters. The leading candidate, MinIO, is\n19\tAGPL-3.0 licensed; redistribution terms must be cleared before any productization\n20\twork can ship, and the outcome may force a different upstream.\n21\t\n22\t## High-Level Requirements\n23\t\n24\t| ID | Priority | Requirement |\n25\t|-------|----------|-------------|\n26\t| HLR-1 | P0 | Legal review of redistributing the candidate object store (MinIO, AGPL-3.0) is completed and documented, including the derivative-work posture for operator integration. This clearance blocks all shipping work. |\n27\t| HLR-2 | P0 | Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible object store through the Platform Operator, with productized images and upgrade lifecycle. |\n28\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Data Science Pipelines and model serving connection defaults can target the bundled store without manual endpoint configuration. |\n29\t| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers enablement, sizing guidance, and the supported/unsupported boundary versus customer-provided storage. |\n30\t\n31\t## Affected Components\n32\t\n33\t- Platform Operator\n34\t- Data Science Pipelines\n35\t- Dashboard\n36\t- Documentation\n37\t\n38\t## Out of Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Replacing customer-provided S3 in connected environments\n41\t- Data migration tooling between stores\n42\t\n43\t## Open Questions\n44\t\n45\t1. If AGPL terms cannot be satisfied for our distribution model, the fallback\n46\t   candidate is an Apache-2.0 alternative (e.g. SeaweedFS) — acceptable, but it\n47\t   restarts image productization.\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6579f8638f8b64e","agent_id":"ab3d3c833fed09e80","session_id":"fb56929f-df9e-42c6-b5d2-389b8632f829","uuid":"9e391e56-a4bf-4ca1-853b-ba8a1aff314f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:14:21.548Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-99ecce3eb56f1b57","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9012"}
