\n    A006 --> A008[BRANCH-A-E008 MinIO Konflux onboarding]\n    E001 --> A009[BRANCH-A-E009 MinIO image productization]\n    A007 --> A009\n    E001 --> B010[BRANCH-B-E010 Fallback repo onboarding]\n    E001 --> B011[BRANCH-B-E011 Fallback license validation]\n    B010 --> B012[BRANCH-B-E012 Fallback Konflux onboarding]\n    E001 --> B013[BRANCH-B-E013 Fallback image productization]\n    B011 --> B013\n```\n\nNote: in each branch, the image-productization epic (E009 / E013) runs parallel to the\nKonflux-onboarding epic (E008 / E012) by Rule 10 — the \"build pipeline green\" acceptance\ncriterion gates first execution, not a DAG edge.\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 → E002 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | HLR-1 states the clearance \"blocks all shipping work\"; operator enablement cannot ship before the redistribution posture is resolved. True gate: `rewrite` (deployment integration re-targets whichever upstream is selected). |\n| E001 → E003 | Rule 3 | HLR-1 blocks all shipping work; although the S3 API surface is the same either way, shipping the default is gated on clearance. Gate impact: `add_remediation` (defaults retarget the selected upstream's endpoint). |\n| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 | Same as E003, for model serving defaults. |\n| E002 ∥ E003 | Rules 13/14 | Different repos, no shared build artifact — the bundled store endpoint is a configuration reference (AC gate on E003), not a build-against artifact. |\n| E002 ∥ E004 | Rules 13/14 | Same configuration-reference reasoning for model serving. |\n| E003 ∥ E004 | Rule 1/14 | Different components (Data Science Pipelines vs model serving), different repos, no shared artifacts. |\n| E002 → E005, E003 → E005, E004 → E005 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring is blocked by ALL Implementation epics; docs describe what was built. Docs priority does not propagate upstream (docs-authoring priority exception). |\n| E001 → BRANCH-*-E006/E007/E010/E011 | Rules 3, 2