ph TD\n63\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9012-E001 Legal review] --> A006[BRANCH-A-E006 MinIO repo onboarding]\n64\t    E001 --> A007[BRANCH-A-E007 MinIO license validation]\n65\t    A006 --> A008[BRANCH-A-E008 MinIO Konflux onboarding]\n66\t    E001 --> A009[BRANCH-A-E009 MinIO image productization]\n67\t    A007 --> A009\n68\t    E001 --> B010[BRANCH-B-E010 Fallback repo onboarding]\n69\t    E001 --> B011[BRANCH-B-E011 Fallback license validation]\n70\t    B010 --> B012[BRANCH-B-E012 Fallback Konflux onboarding]\n71\t    E001 --> B013[BRANCH-B-E013 Fallback image productization]\n72\t    B011 --> B013\n73\t```\n74\t\n75\tNote: in each branch, the image-productization epic (E009 / E013) runs parallel to the\n76\tKonflux-onboarding epic (E008 / E012) by Rule 10 — the \"build pipeline green\" acceptance\n77\tcriterion gates first execution, not a DAG edge.\n78\t\n79\t## DAG Justification\n80\t\n81\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n82\t|------|------|-----------|\n83\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | HLR-1 states the clearance \"blocks all shipping work\"; operator enablement cannot ship before the redistribution posture is resolved. True gate: `rewrite` (deployment integration re-targets whichever upstream is selected). |\n84\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 3 | HLR-1 blocks all shipping work; although the S3 API surface is the same either way, shipping the default is gated on clearance. Gate impact: `add_remediation` (defaults retarget the selected upstream's endpoint). |\n85\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 | Same as E003, for model serving defaults. |\n86\t| E002 ∥ E003 | Rules 13/14 | Different repos, no shared build artifact — the bundled store endpoint is a configuration reference (AC gate on E003), not a build-against artifact. |\n87\t| E002 ∥ E004 | Rules 13/14 | Same configuration-reference reasoning for model serving. |\n88\t| E003 ∥ E004 | Rule 1/14 | Different components (Data Science Pipelines vs model serving), different repos, no shared artifacts. |\n89\t| E002 → E005, E003 → E005, E004 → E005 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring is blocked by ALL Implementation epics; docs describe what was built. Docs priority does not propagate upstream (docs-authoring priority exception). |\n90\t| E001 → BRANCH-*-E006/E007/E010/E011 | Rules 3, 20 | New component not in architecture context: onboarding chain starts only after the legal outcome selects the upstream. repo-onboarding ∥ license-validation (Rule 7). |\n91\t| BRANCH-*-E006 → BRANCH-*-E008 | Rule 5 | konflux-onboarding requires the repo to exist; always serial. |\n92\t| BRANCH-*-E007 → BRANCH-*-E009/E013 | Rule 9 | license-validation → general implementation serial (license failures change dependencies/approach). |\n93\t| BRANCH-*-E008 ∥ BRANCH-*-E009/E013 | Rule 10 | Konflux config is independent of image-build code; NO blocking edge in either direction — enforced by \"build pipeline green\" AC on the productization epic. |\n94\t| No edge: productization → E002 | Rules 13, 10 | The productized image digest consumed by the operator is a configuration reference: E002 gets a \"pinned image digest available\" AC, not a dependency. Also, main-plan epics must not depend on branch epics. |\n95\t\n96\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n97\t\n98\t| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n99\t|-----|----------|-------|\n100\t| HLR-1 (P0): Legal review of redistributing MinIO (AGPL-3.0), documented, incl. derivative-work posture | P0 | E001 |\n101\t| HLR-2 (P0): Admin-enableable bundled S3 store via Platform Operator, productized images, upgrade lifecycle | P0 | E002, BRANCH-A-E006..E009, BRANCH-B-E010..E013 |\n102\t| HLR-3 (P1): DSP and model serving connection defaults target the bundled store | P1 | E003, E004 |\n103\t| HLR-4 (P2): Documentation (enablement, sizing, supported/unsupported boundary) | P2 | E005 |\n104\t\n105\tAll HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n106\t\n107\tNote on E005 priority: HLR-4 is P2, but the docs-authoring priority exception derives\n108\tpriority from the strategy frontmatter (`priority: Major` → P1). Docs priority does not\n109\tpropagate to upstream implementations.\n110\t\n111\t## Component Mapping Notes\n112\t\n113\t- The bundled S3-compatible object store (MinIO / SeaweedFS) is not in\n114\t  `.context/rhai-components.txt` and has no architecture-context file — it is a new\n115\t  component delivered through the Platform Operator. Per the component-name constraint,\n116\t  all store-related epics use the closest canonical component: **Platform Operator**.\n117\t- Affected Components lists \"Dashboard\", but no HLR or described change covers a\n118\t  Dashboard code change. Dashboard is treated as a **passive component**: validation that\n119\t  Dashboard views continue to function against the bundled store is an acceptance\n120\t  criterion on E003 (pipelines views) and E004 (serving views) — the nearest active\n121\t  components. No separate Dashboard epic is generated.\n122\t- HLR-3 explicitly covers \"model serving connection defaults\", but no serving component\n123\t  appears in Affected Components. E004 was created for full HLR coverage using the\n124\t  parent-level canonical component \"Serving Runtimes\" (no architecture-context file\n125\t  exists for KServe or Serving Runtimes). Flagged as a health warning below.\n126\t\n127\t## Health Warnings\n128\t\n129\t1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted Teams\n130\t   table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no\n131\t   Non-Functional Requirements. Team assignments were inferred (RHOAI Platform Operator,\n132\t   RHOAI Pipelines per architecture context, RHOAI Model Serving, RHOAI Docs, Legal).\n133\t   Per-epic acceptance criteria were derived from HLR text.\n134\t2. **Affected Components vs HLR mismatch**: Dashboard is listed as affected but has no\n135\t   corresponding requirement; model serving has a requirement (HLR-3) but is not listed\n136\t   as affected. Treated as passive and added respectively (see Component Mapping Notes).\n137\t3. **Scope trap — carried-fork support burden**: \"productized images and upgrade\n138\t   lifecycle\" implies ongoing CVE/patch maintenance of a midstream fork of the selected\n139\t   upstream. The strategy does not budget this; the productization branch epics carry an\n140\t   upgrade-path acceptance criterion, but long-term maintenance ownership is unassigned.\n141\t4. **Branch B candidate is tentative**: the strategy names SeaweedFS only as an example\n142\t   (\"e.g. SeaweedFS\"). If the legal review forces the fallback, the specific Apache-2.0\n143\t   upstream should be confirmed as the first step of Branch B (noted in BRANCH-B-E010);\n144\t   this does not change the epic structure.\n145\t\n146\t## Tiered Delivery\n147\t\n148\tNot applied as a Tier 1/Tier 2 split on external dependency timing. The upstream is\n149\tconsumed, not contributed to (no upstream PR/RFC), so Rule 21 does not generate an\n150\tupstream Implementation epic. The uncertainty here is legal, handled by the E001\n151\tInvestigation with conditional branches: Branch A (MinIO cleared) and Branch B\n152\t(Apache-2.0 fallback, restarts image productization). No partial-value tier is possible\n153\tbefore clearance because HLR-1 blocks all shipping work.\n154\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-877df0809c3b7ca1","agent_id":"a538cad7c42de1d50","session_id":"fb56929f-df9e-42c6-b5d2-389b8632f829","uuid":"9cd10d90-1d51-4526-8954-537b186c043d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:24:05.489Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba29107dd3b954f5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
