{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a93fd16ead7bf715","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9012-E002\n3\ttitle: Platform Operator enablement of the bundled S3-compatible object store\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9012\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: RHOAI Platform Operator\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9012-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9012-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If MinIO redistribution is not cleared, re-target the operator\n15\t    deployment integration to the selected Apache-2.0 alternative upstream; the enablement\n16\t    capability scope is unchanged but deployment specifics are rewritten.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: -1\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 0\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 1\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Platform Operator enablement of the bundled S3-compatible object store\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tDeliver the operator-side capability that lets administrators enable a\n39\tsupported, bundled S3-compatible object store on disconnected and PoC clusters,\n40\twith productized images and a managed upgrade lifecycle. This replaces the\n41\tunsupported field practice of installing upstream MinIO ad hoc with a\n42\tplatform-visible, supported capability.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Administrator-facing enablement of the bundled S3-compatible object store\n47\t  through the Platform Operator (opt-in; not enabled by default).\n48\t- Deployment and lifecycle management of the bundled store by the operator,\n49\t  consuming the productized store container image.\n50\t- Upgrade lifecycle for the bundled store across platform upgrades.\n51\t- Wiring that allows other platform components to discover and target the\n52\t  bundled store's endpoint without manual configuration.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- An administrator can enable (and disable) the bundled S3-compatible object\n57\t  store through the Platform Operator on a disconnected cluster.\n58\t- When enabled, the store runs from the productized image; the pinned image\n59\t  digest of the productized store is available at wiring time (configuration\n60\t  reference — the operator integration does not block on, and is not blocked\n61\t  by, the image productization work; each proceeds in parallel).\n62\t- The bundled store is not enabled by default; clusters without it behave\n63\t  exactly as before (no regression for customer-provided storage).\n64\t- The upgrade lifecycle is exercised: the bundled store survives a platform\n65\t  upgrade without data loss or manual reconfiguration.\n66\t- The store's S3 endpoint is usable by platform components on the same\n67\t  cluster without manual endpoint entry.\n68\t- The build pipeline for any repository touched by this epic is green.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-2 (P0): Administrators can enable a supported, bundled S3-compatible\n73\t  object store through the Platform Operator, with productized images and\n74\t  upgrade lifecycle.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-877df0809c3b7ca1","agent_id":"a538cad7c42de1d50","session_id":"fb56929f-df9e-42c6-b5d2-389b8632f829","uuid":"9ca8fc9d-6cff-4967-b3c2-9466aa046fee","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:24:11.328Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a93fd16ead7bf715","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
