{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e2aa79905b548a0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9012\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9012 (Bundle an S3-compatible object store for disconnected installs)\n10\t\n11\t## Triage\n12\t\n13\tFull decomposition (not below-threshold, not docs-only). The strategy spans multiple\n14\tcomponents and teams (legal, Platform Operator, Data Science Pipelines, model serving,\n15\tdocumentation) and contains a genuine gating unknown (AGPL-3.0 redistribution clearance)\n16\twhose bounded outcome changes what the productization work targets.\n17\t\n18\t## Epic List (main plan)\n19\t\n20\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n21\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n22\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E001 | Legal review: redistributing MinIO (AGPL-3.0) in the product distribution | Investigation | Legal | P0 |\n23\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E002 | Platform Operator enablement of the bundled S3-compatible object store | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E003 | Data Science Pipelines connection defaults for the bundled store | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P1 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E004 | Model serving connection defaults for the bundled store | Implementation | RHOAI Model Serving | P1 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E005 | Documentation: enablement, sizing, and support boundary for the bundled store | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Docs | P1 |\n27\t\n28\t### Branch epics (conditional, gated by E001 outcome)\n29\t\n30\tThe legal review has two bounded outcomes. The upstream image-productization chain\n31\t(midstream fork, license scan, Konflux pipeline, productized image) targets a different\n32\tupstream depending on the outcome, so it is decomposed as conditional branches attached\n33\tto the Investigation:\n34\t\n35\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority | Branch |\n36\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|--------|\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-A-E006 | Midstream repo onboarding for MinIO | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | A (AGPL cleared) |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-A-E007 | License validation of MinIO and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | A |\n39\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-A-E008 | Konflux onboarding for the productized MinIO image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | A |\n40\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-A-E009 | Productized MinIO container image with upgrade lifecycle | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | A |\n41\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-B-E010 | Midstream repo onboarding for the Apache-2.0 fallback object store | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | B (AGPL not cleared) |\n42\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-B-E011 | License validation of the fallback store and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | B |\n43\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-B-E012 | Konflux onboarding for the productized fallback store image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | B |\n44\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-B-E013 | Productized fallback-store container image with upgrade lifecycle | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | B |\n45\t\n46\t## Dependency DAG (main plan)\n47\t\n48\t```mermaid\n49\tgraph TD\n50\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9012-E001 Legal review] --> E002[RHAISTRAT-9012-E002 Operator enablement]\n51\t    E001 --> E003[RHAISTRAT-9012-E003 DSP defaults]\n52\t    E001 --> E004[RHAISTRAT-9012-E004 Serving defaults]\n53\t    E002 --> E005[RHAISTRAT-9012-E005 Documentation]\n54\t    E003 --> E005\n55\t    E004 --> E005\n56\t```\n57\t\n58\t### Branch DAGs (not main-plan nodes; excluded from critical path)\n59\t\n60\t```mermaid\n61\tgraph TD\n62\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9012-E001 Legal review] --> A006[BRANCH-A-E006 MinIO repo onboarding]\n63\t    E001 --> A007[BRANCH-A-E007 MinIO license validation]\n64\t    A006 --> A008[BRANCH-A-E008 MinIO Konflux onboarding]\n65\t    E001 --> A009[BRANCH-A-E009 MinIO image productization]\n66\t    A007 --> A009\n67\t    E001 --> B010[BRANCH-B-E010 Fallback repo onboarding]\n68\t    E001 --> B011[BRANCH-B-E011 Fallback license validation]\n69\t    B010 --> B012[BRANCH-B-E012 Fallback Konflux onboarding]\n70\t    E001 --> B013[BRANCH-B-E013 Fallback image productization]\n71\t    B011 --> B013\n72\t```\n73\t\n74\tNote: in each branch, the image-productization epic (E009 / E013) runs parallel to the\n75\tKonflux-onboarding epic (E008 / E012) by Rule 10 — the \"build pipeline green\" acceptance\n76\tcriterion gates first execution, not a DAG edge.\n77\t\n78\t## DAG Justification\n79\t\n80\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n81\t|------|------|-----------|\n82\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | HLR-1 states the clearance \"blocks all shipping work\"; operator enablement cannot ship before the redistribution posture is resolved. True gate: `rewrite` (deployment integration re-targets whichever upstream is selected). |\n83\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 3 | HLR-1 blocks all shipping work; although the S3 API surface is the same either way, shipping the default is gated on clearance. Gate impact: `add_remediation` (defaults retarget the selected upstream's endpoint). |\n84\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 | Same as E003, for model serving defaults. |\n85\t| E002 ∥ E003 | Rules 13/14 | Different repos, no shared build artifact — the bundled store endpoint is a configuration reference (AC gate on E003), not a build-against artifact. |\n86\t| E002 ∥ E004 | Rules 13/14 | Same configuration-reference reasoning for model serving. |\n87\t| E003 ∥ E004 | Rule 1/14 | Different components (Data Science Pipelines vs model serving), different repos, no shared artifacts. |\n88\t| E002 → E005, E003 → E005, E004 → E005 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring is blocked by ALL Implementation epics; docs describe what was built. Docs priority does not propagate upstream (docs-authoring priority exception). |\n89\t| E001 → BRANCH-*-E006/E007/E010/E011 | Rules 3, 20 | New component not in architecture context: onboarding chain starts only after the legal outcome selects the upstream. repo-onboarding ∥ license-validation (Rule 7). |\n90\t| BRANCH-*-E006 → BRANCH-*-E008 | Rule 5 | konflux-onboarding requires the repo to exist; always serial. |\n91\t| BRANCH-*-E007 → BRANCH-*-E009/E013 | Rule 9 | license-validation → general implementation serial (license failures change dependencies/approach). |\n92\t| BRANCH-*-E008 ∥ BRANCH-*-E009/E013 | Rule 10 | Konflux config is independent of image-build code; NO blocking edge in either direction — enforced by \"build pipeline green\" AC on the productization epic. |\n93\t| No edge: productization → E002 | Rules 13, 10 | The productized image digest consumed by the operator is a configuration reference: E002 gets a \"pinned image digest available\" AC, not a dependency. Also, main-plan epics must not depend on branch epics. |\n94\t\n95\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n96\t\n97\t| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n98\t|-----|----------|-------|\n99\t| HLR-1 (P0): Legal review of redistributing MinIO (AGPL-3.0), documented, incl. derivative-work posture | P0 | E001 |\n100\t| HLR-2 (P0): Admin-enableable bundled S3 store via Platform Operator, productized images, upgrade lifecycle | P0 | E002, BRANCH-A-E006..E009, BRANCH-B-E010..E013 |\n101\t| HLR-3 (P1): DSP and model serving connection defaults target the bundled store | P1 | E003, E004 |\n102\t| HLR-4 (P2): Documentation (enablement, sizing, supported/unsupported boundary) | P2 | E005 |\n103\t\n104\tAll HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n105\t\n106\tNote on E005 priority: HLR-4 is P2, but the docs-authoring priority exception derives\n107\tpriority from the strategy frontmatter (`priority: Major` → P1). Docs priority does not\n108\tpropagate to upstream implementations.\n109\t\n110\t## Component Mapping Notes\n111\t\n112\t- The bundled S3-compatible object store (MinIO / SeaweedFS) is not in\n113\t  `.context/rhai-components.txt` and has no architecture-context file — it is a new\n114\t  component delivered through the Platform Operator. Per the component-name constraint,\n115\t  all store-related epics use the closest canonical component: **Platform Operator**.\n116\t- Affected Components lists \"Dashboard\", but no HLR or described change covers a\n117\t  Dashboard code change. Dashboard is treated as a **passive component**: validation that\n118\t  Dashboard views continue to function against the bundled store is an acceptance\n119\t  criterion on E003 (pipelines views) and E004 (serving views) — the nearest active\n120\t  components. No separate Dashboard epic is generated.\n121\t- HLR-3 explicitly covers \"model serving connection defaults\", but no serving component\n122\t  appears in Affected Components. E004 was created for full HLR coverage using the\n123\t  parent-level canonical component \"Serving Runtimes\" (no architecture-context file\n124\t  exists for KServe or Serving Runtimes). Flagged as a health warning below.\n125\t\n126\t## Health Warnings\n127\t\n128\t1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted Teams\n129\t   table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no\n130\t   Non-Functional Requirements. Team assignments were inferred (RHOAI Platform Operator,\n131\t   RHOAI Pipelines per architecture context, RHOAI Model Serving, RHOAI Docs, Legal).\n132\t   Per-epic acceptance criteria were derived from HLR text.\n133\t2. **Affected Components vs HLR mismatch**: Dashboard is listed as affected but has no\n134\t   corresponding requirement; model serving has a requirement (HLR-3) but is not listed\n135\t   as affected. Treated as passive and added respectively (see Component Mapping Notes).\n136\t3. **Scope trap — carried-fork support burden**: \"productized images and upgrade\n137\t   lifecycle\" implies ongoing CVE/patch maintenance of a midstream fork of the selected\n138\t   upstream. The strategy does not budget this; the productization branch epics carry an\n139\t   upgrade-path acceptance criterion, but long-term maintenance ownership is unassigned.\n140\t4. **Branch B candidate is tentative**: the strategy names SeaweedFS only as an example\n141\t   (\"e.g. SeaweedFS\"). If the legal review forces the fallback, the specific Apache-2.0\n142\t   upstream should be confirmed as the first step of Branch B (noted in BRANCH-B-E010);\n143\t   this does not change the epic structure.\n144\t\n145\t## Tiered Delivery\n146\t\n147\tNot applied as a Tier 1/Tier 2 split on external dependency timing. The upstream is\n148\tconsumed, not contributed to (no upstream PR/RFC), so Rule 21 does not generate an\n149\tupstream Implementation epic. The uncertainty here is legal, handled by the E001\n150\tInvestigation with conditional branches: Branch A (MinIO cleared) and Branch B\n151\t(Apache-2.0 fallback, restarts image productization). No partial-value tier is possible\n152\tbefore clearance because HLR-1 blocks all shipping work.\n153\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8db1aca161d32892","agent_id":"ac67f86ba196777aa","session_id":"fb56929f-df9e-42c6-b5d2-389b8632f829","uuid":"b0286444-9bbb-4d07-91d6-f9c6a2578508","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:28:35.405Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e2aa79905b548a0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
