{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a36be22f4d8a23b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9012-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Legal review: redistributing MinIO (AGPL-3.0) in the product distribution'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9012\n5\tcomponent: Platform Operator\n6\tteam: Legal\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Legal review: redistributing MinIO (AGPL-3.0) in the product distribution\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolve the licensing uncertainty that blocks all shipping work for the bundled\n30\tS3-compatible object store. Legal reviews whether MinIO (AGPL-3.0) can be\n31\tredistributed as part of the product distribution for disconnected installs,\n32\tincluding the derivative-work posture for integrating it with the platform\n33\toperator (bundling, deploying, and managing MinIO from our operator). The\n34\toutcome is a documented clearance decision.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Legal analysis of AGPL-3.0 redistribution terms under the product's\n39\t  distribution model for disconnected / PoC clusters.\n40\t- Explicit determination of the derivative-work posture for operator\n41\t  integration: whether deploying and managing MinIO from the platform operator\n42\t  creates obligations (source availability, notices, offer requirements) and\n43\t  what satisfying them requires.\n44\t- Documented decision with the conditions of clearance, or a documented\n45\t  finding that redistribution is not acceptable.\n46\t- If redistribution is not acceptable: confirmation of the fallback candidate\n47\t  (an Apache-2.0 alternative, e.g. SeaweedFS) as the productization target.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- The legal review is completed and documented, covering redistribution terms\n52\t  and the derivative-work posture for operator integration (HLR-1).\n53\t- The decision record states, unambiguously, whether MinIO may be bundled, and\n54\t  under what conditions.\n55\t- If clearance is denied, the record identifies the fallback upstream and\n56\t  notes that image productization restarts against it.\n57\t- The outcome is communicated to the platform operator, pipelines, and model\n58\t  serving teams so downstream work can proceed.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-1 (P0): Legal review of redistributing the candidate object store\n63\t  (MinIO, AGPL-3.0) is completed and documented, including the derivative-work\n64\t  posture for operator integration.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8db1aca161d32892","agent_id":"ac67f86ba196777aa","session_id":"fb56929f-df9e-42c6-b5d2-389b8632f829","uuid":"c55f1bf7-84ff-40f0-85d0-66ef8f1dbcb9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T00:28:50.680Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a36be22f4d8a23b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9012 decomposition"}
