{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adc68d08814135fe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9012\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9012 (Bundle an S3-compatible object store for disconnected installs)\n10\t\n11\t## Triage\n12\t\n13\tFull decomposition (not below-threshold, not docs-only). The strategy spans multiple\n14\tcomponents and teams (legal, Platform Operator, Data Science Pipelines, model serving,\n15\tdocumentation) and contains a genuine gating unknown (AGPL-3.0 redistribution clearance)\n16\twhose bounded outcome changes what the productization work targets.\n17\t\n18\t## Epic List (main plan)\n19\t\n20\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n21\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n22\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E001 | Legal review: redistributing MinIO (AGPL-3.0) in the product distribution | Investigation | Legal | P0 |\n23\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E002 | Platform Operator enablement of the bundled S3-compatible object store | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E003 | Data Science Pipelines connection defaults for the bundled store | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P1 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E004 | Model serving connection defaults for the bundled store | Implementation | RHOAI Model Serving | P1 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-E005 | Documentation: enablement, sizing, and support boundary for the bundled store | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Docs | P1 |\n27\t\n28\t### Branch epics (conditional, gated by E001 outcome)\n29\t\n30\tThe legal review has two bounded outcomes. The upstream image-productization chain\n31\t(midstream fork, license scan, Konflux pipeline, productized image) targets a different\n32\tupstream depending on the outcome, so it is decomposed as conditional branches attached\n33\tto the Investigation:\n34\t\n35\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority | Branch |\n36\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|--------|\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-A-E006 | Midstream repo onboarding for MinIO | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | A (AGPL cleared) |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-A-E007 | License validation of MinIO and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | A |\n39\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-A-E008 | Konflux onboarding for the productized MinIO image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | A |\n40\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-A-E009 | Productized MinIO container image with upgrade lifecycle | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | A |\n41\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-B-E010 | Midstream repo onboarding for the Apache-2.0 fallback object store | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | B (AGPL not cleared) |\n42\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-B-E011 | License validation of the fallback store and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | B |\n43\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-B-E012 | Konflux onboarding for the productized fallback store image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | B |\n44\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-B-E013 | Productized fallback-store container image with upgrade lifecycle | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | B |\n45\t\n46\t## Dependency DAG (main plan)\n47\t\n48\t```mermaid\n49\tgraph TD\n50\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9012-E001 Legal review] --> E002[RHAISTRAT-9012-E002 Operator enablement]\n51\t    E001 --> E003[RHAISTRAT-9012-E003 DSP defaults]\n52\t    E001 --> E004[RHAISTRAT-9012-E004 Serving defaults]\n53\t    E002 --> E005[RHAISTRAT-9012-E005 Documentation]\n54\t    E003 --> E005\n55\t    E004 --> E005\n56\t```\n57\t\n58\t### Branch DAGs (not main-plan nodes; excluded from critical path)\n59\t\n60\t```mermaid\n61\tgraph TD\n62\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9012-E001 Legal review] --> A006[BRANCH-A-E006 MinIO repo onboarding]\n63\t    E001 --> A007[BRANCH-A-E007 MinIO license validation]\n64\t    A006 --> A008[BRANCH-A-E008 MinIO Konflux onboarding]\n65\t    E001 --> A009[BRANCH-A-E009 MinIO image productization]\n66\t    A007 --> A009\n67\t    A006 --> A009\n68\t    E001 --> B010[BRANCH-B-E010 Fallback repo onboarding]\n69\t    E001 --> B011[BRANCH-B-E011 Fallback license validation]\n70\t    B010 --> B012[BRANCH-B-E012 Fallback Konflux onboarding]\n71\t    E001 --> B013[BRANCH-B-E013 Fallback image productization]\n72\t    B011 --> B013\n73\t    B010 --> B013\n74\t```\n75\t\n76\tNote: in each branch, the image-productization epic (E009 / E013) runs parallel to the\n77\tKonflux-onboarding epic (E008 / E012) by Rule 10 — the \"build pipeline green\" acceptance\n78\tcriterion gates first execution, not a DAG edge. The repo-onboarding epic is serial\n79\tbefore both: Konflux onboarding requires the repo to exist, and the productization work\n80\tis authored in and built from that repository.\n81\t\n82\t## DAG Justification\n83\t\n84\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n85\t|------|------|-----------|\n86\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | HLR-1 states the clearance \"blocks all shipping work\"; operator enablement cannot ship before the redistribution posture is resolved. True gate: `rewrite` (deployment integration re-targets whichever upstream is selected). |\n87\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 3 | HLR-1 blocks all shipping work; although the S3 API surface is the same either way, shipping the default is gated on clearance. Gate impact: `add_remediation` (defaults retarget the selected upstream's endpoint). |\n88\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 | Same as E003, for model serving defaults. |\n89\t| E002 ∥ E003 | Rules 13/14 | Different repos, no shared build artifact — the bundled store endpoint is a configuration reference (AC gate on E003), not a build-against artifact. |\n90\t| E002 ∥ E004 | Rules 13/14 | Same configuration-reference reasoning for model serving. |\n91\t| E003 ∥ E004 | Rule 1/14 | Different components (Data Science Pipelines vs model serving), different repos, no shared artifacts. |\n92\t| E002 → E005, E003 → E005, E004 → E005 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring is blocked by ALL Implementation epics; docs describe what was built. Docs priority does not propagate upstream (docs-authoring priority exception). |\n93\t| E001 → BRANCH-*-E006/E007/E010/E011 | Rules 3, 20 | New component not in architecture context: onboarding chain starts only after the legal outcome selects the upstream. repo-onboarding ∥ license-validation (Rule 7). |\n94\t| BRANCH-*-E006 → BRANCH-*-E008 | Rule 5 | konflux-onboarding requires the repo to exist; always serial. |\n95\t| BRANCH-*-E006/E010 → BRANCH-*-E009/E013 | Rule 4 (data/artifact dependency) | The image productization (build recipe, base-image and labeling conventions, version pinning) is authored in and built from the midstream repository the repo-onboarding epic creates; the productization cannot start before the repo exists. Not a Rule 10 violation: repo-onboarding vs general implementation is not a mandated-parallel pair (only konflux-onboarding vs general implementation is). |\n96\t| BRANCH-*-E007 → BRANCH-*-E009/E013 | Rule 9 | license-validation → general implementation serial (license failures change dependencies/approach). |\n97\t| BRANCH-*-E008 ∥ BRANCH-*-E009/E013 | Rule 10 | Konflux config is independent of image-build code; NO blocking edge in either direction — enforced by \"build pipeline green\" AC on the productization epic. |\n98\t| No edge: productization → E002 | Rules 13, 10 | The productized image digest consumed by the operator is a configuration reference: E002 gets a \"pinned image digest available\" AC, not a dependency. Also, main-plan epics must not depend on branch epics. |\n99\t\n100\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n101\t\n102\t| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n103\t|-----|----------|-------|\n104\t| HLR-1 (P0):