the Investigation:\n35\t\n36\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority | Branch |\n37\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|--------|\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-A-E006 | Midstream repo onboarding for MinIO | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | A (AGPL cleared) |\n39\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-A-E007 | License validation of MinIO and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | A |\n40\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-A-E008 | Konflux onboarding for the productized MinIO image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | A |\n41\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-A-E009 | Productized MinIO container image with upgrade lifecycle | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | A |\n42\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-B-E010 | Midstream repo onboarding for the Apache-2.0 fallback object store | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | B (AGPL not cleared) |\n43\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-B-E011 | License validation of the fallback store and transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | B |\n44\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-B-E012 | Konflux onboarding for the productized fallback store image | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | B |\n45\t| RHAISTRAT-9012-BRANCH-B-E013 | Productized fallback-store container image with upgrade lifecycle | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 | B |\n46\t\n47\t## Dependency DAG (main plan)\n48\t\n49\t```mermaid\n50\tgraph TD\n51\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9012-E001 Legal review] --> E002[RHAISTRAT-9012-E002 Operator enablement]\n52\t    E001 --> E003[RHAISTRAT-9012-E003 DSP defaults]\n53\t    E001 --> E004[RHAISTRAT-9012-E004 Serving defaults]\n54\t    E002 --> E005[RHAISTRAT-9012-E005 Documentation]\n55\t    E003 --> E005\n56\t    E004 --> E005\n57\t```\n58\t\n59\t### Branch DAGs (not main-plan nodes; excluded from critical path)\n60\t\n61\t```mermaid\n62\tgraph TD\n63\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9012-E001 Legal review] --> A006[BRANCH-A-E006 MinIO repo onboarding]\n64\t    E001 --> A007[BRANCH-A-E007 MinIO license validation]\n65\t    A006 --> A008[BRANCH-A-E008 MinIO Konflux onboarding]\n66\t    E001 --> A008\n67\t    E001 --> A009[BRANCH-A-E009 MinIO image productization]\n68\t    A007 --> A009\n69\t    A006 --> A009\n70\t    E001 --> B010[BRANCH-B-E010 Fallback repo onboarding]\n71\t    E001 --> B011[BRANCH-B-E011 Fallback license validation]\n72\t    B010 --> B012[BRANCH-B-E012 Fallback Konflux onboarding]\n73\t    E001 --> B012\n74\t    E001 --> B013[BRANCH-B-E013 Fallback image productization]\n75\t    B011 --> B013\n76\t    B010 --> B013\n77\t```\n78\t\n79\tNote: in each branch, the image-productization epic (E009 / E013) runs parallel to the\n80\tKonflux-onboarding epic (E008 / E012) by Rule 10 — the \"build pipeline green\" acceptance\n81\tcriterion gates first execution, not a DAG edge. The repo-onboarding epic is serial\n82\tbefore both: Konflux onboarding requires the repo to exist, and the productization work\n83\tis authored in and built from that repository.\n84\t\n85\t## DAG Justification\n86\t\n87\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n88\t|------|------|-----------|\n89\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | HLR-1 states the clearance \"blocks all shipping work\"; operator enablement cannot ship before the redistribution posture is resolved. True gate: `rewrite` (deployment integration re-targets whichever upstream is selected). |\n90\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 3 | HLR-1 blocks all shipping work; although the S3 API surface is the same either way, shipping the default is gated on clearance. Gate impact: `add_remediation` (defaults retarget the selected upstream's endpoint). |\n91\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 | Same as E003, for model serving defaults. |\n92\t| E002 ∥ E003 | Rules 13/14 | Different repos, no shared build artifact — the bundled store endpoint is a configuration reference (AC gate on E003), not a